    "title": "Downtown Chill Plant Blows $300 Million Hole In San Antonio's Marvel Makeover - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Javi Gonzalez ,\n11 hours ago San Antonio’s big downtown makeover just got hit with a 300 million dollar cold splash of reality. The city and San Antonio Water System (SAWS) have quietly pulled the plug on plans to move the downtown chilled water plant after a feasibility review pegged the price tag at more than $300 million, roughly triple earlier expectations. Scrapping the relocation knocks out a key piece of the original Project Marvel footprint and forces planners to rethink how a Spurs arena, convention center upgrades and new hospitality space will be built around the existing utility instead of on top of it. Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak 1",
